  "term": "cerebral stimulation",
  "definition": "In this historical source, cerebral stimulation means a direct exciting effect on the brain, inferred when marked agitation appears before paralysis and cannot be explained only by breathing difficulty. It is also linked here with a greater tendency to convulsive or epileptiform attacks.",
